cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite this repository and the associated manuscript."
title: "NBI State-Border Discontinuity Analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhattarai
    given-names: Pawan
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bhattaraipawan/NBI-State-Border-Discontinuities"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible Python workflow for outcome-blind U.S. state-border screening,
  exact geographic discontinuity analysis, matching, robustness checks, and
  climate sensitivity using the 2025 National Bridge Inventory. The finalized
  workflow analyzes the five highest-ranked borders and uses Kansas-Missouri as
  the sole detailed case.
keywords:
  - National Bridge Inventory
  - bridge condition ratings
  - geographic regression discontinuity
  - reproducible research
